 "narration": [
  "I audit green buildings for a living. People picture a clipboard and a few approving nods. It's not that.",
  "Most of the job is finding the gap between what the drawings say and what was actually installed. And there's almost always a gap.",
  "The occupancy sensor that's on the plan, but not on the ceiling. The low-flow fixture swapped late to save a few dollars a unit. The solar array that looks beautiful on paper, and nowhere else.",
  "Nobody here is a villain. A sustainability decision made in a design meeting has to survive a construction site, a budget cut, and subcontractors who've never worked to that standard.",
  "So the job isn't approving good intentions. It's verifying they survived contact with reality.",
  "Certification isn't a trophy. It's proof that something that could easily have been cut, wasn't."
 ],
